<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106095" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῠχ-ηρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lucky, fortunate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				464
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1295a28
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					250
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				305
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>from</i> or <i>by chance,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					7.68
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τ. ἀγαθά</span> the goods
				<i>of fortune,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.6a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i> Aphr. <i><span class="en">
				<u>in Top.</u>
				147.22
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Vit.</u>
					p.27J.
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.35a
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Sign.</u>
					36
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.23f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μικρὰ καὶ τ.</span>
			<i>ordinary</i> trifles (like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ
			τυχόντα</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Zeno Stoic.
				1.70
			</span></i>.</div>
